{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The derivative $h'(x)$ of a function $(h)$ at a point $(x)$ can be viewed as the steepness and direction, or slope, of the function's graph at that point.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Here we see the steepness and direction of the graph of $h$ at the point where $x=-1$:\n\n![graph](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/3ed4753c719b706517995fdac04b198648723c43)","images":{"web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/3ed4753c719b706517995fdac04b198648723c43":{"height":425,"width":425}},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We can see that the graph is constant at $x=-1$, which means the slope must be equal to $0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $h'(-1)=0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Estimate $h'(-1)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n![graph](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/a959f64f807daaaf7830caad2757d237ed8cd0f1)","images":{"web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/a959f64f807daaaf7830caad2757d237ed8cd0f1":{"height":425,"width":425}},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-5$","correct":false},{"content":"$0$","correct":true},{"content":"$5$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$0.2$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-0.2$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
